<h1>TActiveLabel</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveLabel" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveLabel</tt> is the active control counterpart of
<a href="?page=Controls.Label">TLabel</a>. It renders the same markup and adds the
ability to change itself during a callback.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Effect on the browser</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Text</tt></td>
	<td>Replaces the content of the element. The value is written as markup, not escaped, exactly as <tt>TLabel</tt> renders it.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ForControl</tt></td>
	<td>Rewrites the <tt>for</tt> attribute. The element the label renders is decided at render time, so a label that started as a span stays a span for the rest of the request.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
Both updates are subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>.
</p>

